==German==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|gmh|de}} {{term|loch|lang=gmh}}, from {{etyl|goh|de}} {{term|louh|lang=goh}}, from {{etyl|gem-pro|de}} {{m|gem-pro|*laukaz}}. Compare Low German {{term|Look|lang=nds}}, {{term|look|lang=nds}}, Dutch {{term|look|lang=nl}}, English {{term|leek|lang=en}}, Danish {{term|løg|lang=da}}, Swedish {{term|lök|lang=sv}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|[laʊ̯χ]|lang=de}}

===Noun===
{{de-noun|m||Lauche}}

# [[leek]]

====Usage notes====
''Porree'' is dominant in northern and central Germany, while ''Lauch'' is dominant in southern Germany and Switzerland; in Austria, neither is dominant.

